    {
      "cve": "CVE-2026-116133",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-116133"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "HTTP::Body versions before 1.23_01 for Perl allow CPU exhaustion via quadratic rescanning of a multipart body with a missing or malformed boundary.\n\nBefore the first part, and between parts, the multipart parser searches the whole buffered body for the next boundary. On a miss it keeps everything and searches again from the start when the next chunk arrives. A body with no boundary, or with a delimiter followed by neither CRLF nor \"--\", is therefore rescanned on every chunk, taking time quadratic in its size.\n\nA remote attacker can exhaust worker CPU with a few such requests.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
      "product_status": {
        "recommended": [
          "openSUSE Tumbleweed:perl-HTTP-Body-0:1.240.0-1.1.aarch64",
          "openSUSE Tumbleweed:perl-HTTP-Body-0:1.240.0-1.1.ppc64le",
