    {
      "cve": "CVE-2026-116134",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-116134"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "HTTP::Body versions before 1.23_01 for Perl allow memory exhaustion via an unbounded multipart part header block.\n\nThe multipart parser takes everything up to the first blank line after a boundary as the part's header block, with no limit on its size or number of lines. Every line is stored in the part's header hash, so a block of short lines costs about 60 bytes of memory per input byte.\n\nA remote attacker can exhaust worker memory with a single request.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
      "product_status": {
        "recommended": [
          "openSUSE Tumbleweed:perl-HTTP-Body-0:1.240.0-1.1.aarch64",
